# What the sdist carries, beyond what setuptools_scm's file finder offers
# it. The finder offers every git-tracked file, which is the right default
# for a repository of source and documentation and the wrong one for
# anything tracked that describes how the project was built rather than
# what it is.
#
# docs/plans/ is exactly that. The plans, their phases and the audits
# filed under them (including the 1.2MB of per-merge diffs the push audit
# in docs/plans/PLAN-library-api-and-collection-phase-06-push-audit.md
# recorded) are the project's working history. They stay in git, where a
# reader checking why the code is shaped the way it is can find them, but
# nobody installing from source needs them, and they only grow: every new
# plan made the sdist bigger without changing a line of what it builds.
# The user-facing documentation elsewhere under docs/ still ships.
prune docs/plans
